WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:14,910
By sun needs some orthodontic work done and I wondered if metal braces or

00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:20,410
visoline is the better option. Is there one that is less toxic to have it as

00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:32,980
most? Well, I think the visoline is less toxic. It's a plastic tray, but I think

00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:36,940
you're getting less toxins from that than you're getting from metal braces.

00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:42,440
The reason is the metal braces is stainless steel that's only done to your teeth with

00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:50,200
a clamp. You have to use a paste that is going to basically cement them onto the

00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:57,440
teeth. So there's toxins that are involved with that. That means said there

00:00:57,440 --> 00:01:02,680
are sometimes that the visoline will work for people. So you have to talk to

00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:07,640
multiple different orthodontics to see what is going to be best for that person's

00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:13,080
mouth because you know depending on what is needed to be done if it's a widened

00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:17,800
palate if you might need to get an expander beforehand. There's just lots of

00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:23,120
different things that go on with that. I'm not going to give advice about

00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:28,360
orthodontic work, but from a toxicity level I think you're better off with the

00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:30,760
visoline.

